export default {"format":"cadcraft-help","version":1,"app":"partcraft","addon":"factory","name":"Factory floor","sections":{"start":"Getting started","tasks":"Walkthroughs","switching":"Coming from other software","reference":"Reference","trouble":"Troubleshooting and limits"},"topics":[{"slug":"factory-part","scope":"addon:factory","title":"Factory floor: send CAM programs to the job queue","summary":"Hand a program posted in Manufacture to the factory job queue in ModelCraft, or save it as a job file.","section":"tasks","order":10,"keywords":["factory","job queue","cam","post","g-code","nc program","send to machine"],"headings":[{"id":"hand-a-program-to-the-factory","text":"Hand a program to the factory","level":2}],"html":"\u003Ch2 id=\"hand-a-program-to-the-factory\"\u003EHand a program to the factory\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Col\u003E\u003Cli\u003EOpen \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003ESettings\u003C/span\u003E, then \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EAdd-ons\u003C/span\u003E, and switch on \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EFactory floor\u003C/span\u003E. A \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EFactory floor\u003C/span\u003E tab appears in the right panel.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EIn \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EManufacture\u003C/span\u003E, post the program as usual (\u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EPost…\u003C/span\u003E or \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003ESend to a machine…\u003C/span\u003E). The tab shows the last program posted, and for which control.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EChoose \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EAdd to the factory job queue\u003C/span\u003E. In ModelCraft&#039;s \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EFactory floor\u003C/span\u003E panel, \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003ETake jobs from PartCraft\u003C/span\u003E brings it into the queue, where you pick the machine and send it.\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ol\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe hand-over works between apps open in the same browser. Otherwise use \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003ESave as a job file\u003C/span\u003E and, in ModelCraft, \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EOpen a job file…\u003C/span\u003E.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThis tab never sends a program or starts a machine. Sending is done from the queue through CadCraft Studio&#039;s Send to a machine, which uploads the file; you start it at the machine. Not a safety system.\u003C/p\u003E","text":"Hand a program to the factory Open Settings, then Add-ons, and switch on Factory floor. A Factory floor tab appears in the right panel. In Manufacture, post the program as usual (Post… or Send to a machine…). The tab shows the last program posted, and for which control. Choose Add to the factory job queue. In ModelCraft's Factory floor panel, Take jobs from PartCraft brings it into the queue, where you pick the machine and send it. The hand-over works between apps open in the same browser. Otherwise use Save as a job file and, in ModelCraft, Open a job file…. This tab never sends a program or starts a machine. Sending is done from the queue through CadCraft Studio's Send to a machine, which uploads the file; you start it at the machine. Not a safety system."}]};
